+Feature: Todo Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by status
+  So that I can see only the todos I care about
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And todos "Buy groceries", "Walk the dog", "Do laundry" exist
+    And "Buy groceries" is completed
+
+  Rule: Default route shows all todos
+
+  Scenario: Showing all todos by default
+    When I navigate to "#/"
+    Then I see 3 todos in the list
+    And the "All" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Filtering to active todos
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then I see 1 todo in the list
+    And the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo in the active filter hides it
+    Given I am on the "#/active" filter
+    When I click the checkbox for "Walk the dog"
+    Then "Walk the dog" is not visible in the list
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Filtering to completed todos
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then I see 1 todo in the list
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a todo in the completed filter hides it
+    Given I am on the "#/completed" filter
+    When I click the checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then "Buy groceries" is not visible in the list
+
+  Rule: Filter persistence
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted on reload
+    Given I am on the "#/active" filter
+    When I reload the app
+    Then I see 1 todo in the list
+    And the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
